xtreme aggression, likely only called by better hands\n\nReason:\n\nGiven my opponent's passive calling pattern throughout all streets and their river check, I should be cautious. The King on the river is a scare card that could have improved their hand to Kings and Tens (beating my Queens and Tens). My opponent's passive line suggests either a made hand that's trapping, a missed draw, or a weaker made hand afraid of my aggression.\n\nSince I'm already ahead in cumulative chips and this hand represents a marginal value situation, checking back is the prudent choice. It guarantees I see a showdown without risking additional chips in a spot where I'm unlikely to get called by worse hands but could easily be beat by Kings or a full house.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
